      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know that I advocated for merging the pipeline and dynamic state together in a previous CL, but the single-bind approach like this is going to conflict with the changes for YUV AHBs:\n\nCode in https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/297196/34/src/dawn/native/vulkan/CommandBufferVk.cpp#695 has something like:\n\n```\n        typename Pipeline::SpecializedHandles pipelineHandles;\n        DAWN_TRY_ASSIGN(pipelineHandles, lastPipeline-\u003eGetOrCreateSpecializedHandle(std::move(s)));\n\n        DirtyAll();\n\n        VkCommandBuffer commands \u003d recordingContext-\u003ecommandBuffer;\n        vk.CmdBindPipeline(commands, PipelineBindPoint, pipelineHandles.pipeline);\n```\n\nwhere a specialized VkPipeline is created and needs to be bound by the `RunWithSpecialization` code. With `Bind` in this CL tying up both the pipeline and the dynamic state, it becomes harder to change the handle used for the `vkCmdBindPipeline`.\n\nMaybe this function could be `void ApplyDynamicState(command, prevPipeline)`?",
      "revId": "b9709a0ef01574ab7a517d9c9d389de80d8fbfc4",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
